The Mercure hub (internal/mercurehub)
-------------------------------------

This one is not adapted code but a whole program that is linked in. A cairo
binary built in the default way (make build, make static, the releases and
the official image) contains the Mercure.rocks hub,
https://github.com/dunglas/mercure, which serves `$http->mercure()` and
`mercure_publish()`:

    Copyright (C) 2018-present Kévin Dunglas

    This program is free software: you can redistribute it and/or modify
    it under the terms of the GNU Affero General Public License, version 3,
    as published by the Free Software Foundation.

The hub is NOT under Cairo's Apache License 2.0. Its license, the GNU Affero
General Public License version 3 (AGPL-3.0), is in third_party/mercure/LICENSE.
Cairo's own code stays under the Apache License 2.0, which allows it to be
combined with AGPL-3.0 code; a binary that contains the hub is then a
combined work, and whoever conveys that binary, or lets users interact with
it over a network, has the duties of the AGPL-3.0 for it. The sources that
correspond to a released binary are Cairo's at the release's tag
(https://github.com/cairophp/cairo) and the hub's at the version go.mod
names.

A binary without any AGPL code is built with the Go build tag `nomercure`
(`make build TAGS=nomercure`, or CAIRO_TAGS=nomercure for the static
build): it has no hub, refuses `$http->mercure()` and has no
`mercure_publish()`. Only internal/mercurehub imports the hub, and
internal/mercurehub/nohub.go is what such a build compiles instead. The
hub's authors also sell it under commercial terms (https://mercure.rocks).
